    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103887" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηΰσιος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τᾱΰσιος</span></b>  (<i><span class="en">
			Alcm.
			92
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			B.
			5.81
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>idle, vain,
				undertaken to no purpose</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηϋσίη ὁδός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					3.316
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				15.13
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηΰσιον ἔπος</span> an
				<i>idle, rash</i> word, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				540
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ ταΰσιον προΐει ὀϊστόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. πόδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.651
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηϋσίως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					25.230
				</span></i>
			. Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔσιος</span>.</div>
